# NIZAM - environment template for the `caddy` service. TEMPLATE ONLY. NOTHING HERE IS EXECUTED.
#
# Owning contract: PFOS 12 - Two-Agent VPS Deployment & Operations, §2.2.1-§2.2.4 (one public port,
#   automatic TLS, two hostnames, the secret path segment is not the bot token), §3.1 (one
#   environment file per service), §3.2.7 (root-owned, mode-restricted, and read by no other
#   service), §7.6 (this path).
# Spec: .kiro/specs/06-two-agent-vps/ - task 7.3. Contract 12, phase 7. Requirements R6, R23, R24.
# Steering: .kiro/steering/two-agent-vps.md §0b (no deployment particular in a tracked file),
#   §2 (writing this file is permitted, running it is not), §7 (placeholders only, AC09).
#
# Companions: ops/docker-compose.yml declares this file as this service's single env_file, under the
#   placeholder <PROXY_ENV_PATH>; ops/Caddyfile is the configuration whose values these are.
#   Audited by src/server/ops/envTemplates.ts, which every test run re-checks.
#
# HOW TO READ AN ENTRY. Each assignment is preceded by exactly three annotation lines:
#   what:    one line saying what the value is
#   gate:    which human gate in ops/GATE_REGISTER.md supplies it - G1..G8, or `operator` for a
#            value the operator simply chooses, or `build` for a path to an artefact the build emits
#   secret:  yes if disclosing the value would let someone reach or impersonate this deployment
#
# EVERY VALUE IS AN <ANGLE_BRACKET> PLACEHOLDER WHOSE NAME IS ITS OWN ENTRY NAME. There is no
# example value anywhere in this file, no redacted stand-in of the right length, and no comment
# showing a value's shape or width. Steering §0b is categorical, and the practical reason is that a
# plausible-looking example is precisely the thing that gets copied into a real deployment.
#
# THIS SERVICE HOLDS NO AGENT SECRET. It has no bot token, no model key, and no storage credential.
# What it does hold is the two secret webhook path segments, because routing by them is the proxy's
# own job (§2.2.3) and neither agent ever needs to know its own. Read the other direction, which is
# the property that matters: no agent's environment file contains a webhook path segment.

# what: the life agent's site address - no relationship to the finance agent's is assumed (§2.2.3), since a free dynamic-DNS name has no apex to share
# gate: G2
# secret: no
LIFE_HOSTNAME=<LIFE_HOSTNAME>

# what: the finance agent's site address, independent of the life agent's for the same reason
# gate: G2
# secret: no
MONEY_HOSTNAME=<MONEY_HOSTNAME>

# what: the contact address the certificate authority registers for expiry notices
# gate: operator
# secret: no
ACME_CONTACT=<ACME_CONTACT>

# what: the high-entropy path segment that routes the life agent's webhook, generated on the host
# gate: G6
# secret: yes
LIFE_WEBHOOK_PATH=<LIFE_WEBHOOK_PATH>

# what: the high-entropy path segment that routes the finance agent's webhook, generated on the host
# gate: G6
# secret: yes
MONEY_WEBHOOK_PATH=<MONEY_WEBHOOK_PATH>

# what: the port the life agent listens on inside its own network; the proxy's upstream port
# gate: operator
# secret: no
LIFE_CONTAINER_PORT=<LIFE_CONTAINER_PORT>

# what: the port the finance agent listens on inside its own network; the proxy's upstream port
# gate: operator
# secret: no
FINANCE_CONTAINER_PORT=<FINANCE_CONTAINER_PORT>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What is deliberately absent
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. NO KILL SWITCH ENTRY. Contract 12 §8.2 names the two agents, the scheduler, and the backup
#    service as the honourers of the coarse halt, and ops/docker-compose.yml mounts the sentinel
#    volume into exactly those four. The proxy writes nothing and calls no model, so there is
#    nothing for it to halt; giving it a halt entry would imply a writer that does not exist.
#
# 2. NO BOT TOKEN AND NO SECRET-TOKEN VALUE. The provider echoes its secret token on every request
#    and the proxy passes the header through untouched - it neither checks nor consumes it
#    (ops/Caddyfile). The check is the code half of the same guard and lives in the agent
#    (src/server/telegram/auth.ts). A proxy that held the value could compare it, and then the
#    constant-time comparison R11 requires would exist in a place no test covers.
#
# 3. NO REFERENCE TO THE CONSENT CHANNEL. The proxy is on neither internal network, so it has no
#    route to the bus even if a rule were written (ops/BUS_NETWORK_BINDING.md items 2 and 3, R9).
#    An entry naming the bus here would be the first half of such a rule.
